-- BUILT (unit SRM24): dev runs a1, a2 (exit 1), a3 (exit 0); the final-SHA rebuild in REPORT-SRM24.md is the only final evidence.
-- SCOPE (SRM24 audits) of the 6 new theorems: `regWidth_eq_of_hierGate`, `shippedRegWidthLe_of_hierGate` (Tools/ShippingSrm24Width.lean) and, for topshareM / topshareQ, `_shippedRegWidthLe`, `_regsFit_of_hstR_hst1_noW` (Tests/Compiler/Srm24WidthTest.lean).
-- (1) PREMISE TABLE equal to `Tests/Compiler/Srm24AuditExpected.lean` and `scripts/srm24/PREMISES.txt`, `S24THM` marker per theorem, literal count guard (6); three semantic negative fixtures (` ∧ True` on a Prop binder, added data binder, reordered binders), each non-vacuous and rejected.
--     REGENERATION: build Tests.Compiler.Srm24AuditTest, then `python3 -I scripts/srm24/gen_audit.py LOG`.
-- (2) INDEPENDENT FULL-TYPE EXPECTED STATEMENTS `Tests/Compiler/Srm24ExpStmt.lean`, GENERATED by scripts/srm24/gen_exp.py from the Lean text of scripts/srm24/EXPECTED.txt (fixed before any proof): `isDefEq` for the 6 theorems; four wrong expected forms (hW kept, wrong gap, hpost dropped, hwn dropped) are rejected.
--     SOURCE-DERIVED check: each corollary's conclusion is defeq to that of the SRM23 corollary at the shared binders, and the binder-name difference is EXACTLY `hW` removed, nothing added (with a control).
-- (3) ONE WITNESS for each instance theorem; G4 (`ShippedRegWidthLe`) is checked NOT defeq to any Prop binder type of the new theorems (no relabelling), with a control (the premise `hW` of the SRM23 corollary).
-- (4) CLOSURE: standard axioms; forbidden old-form roots (with control); the SRM23 corollary, the generic G4 lemma and core_hierGate_anyAM are in the closures of the corollaries.
set_option Elab.async false
set_option autoImplicit false
section
open Lean Elab Command Meta

namespace Tests.Compiler.Srm24AuditTest

/-- a hand-made MUTATION for the binder audit's control: a theorem whose single hypothesis IS its conclusion -/
theorem wrapper_mutation (p : Prop) (h : p) : p := h


